---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { translations } from '../i18n/translations';

const t = translations.en;
const githubUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GITHUB_URL;
const url = 'https://fntx.modone.me/about/';
const homeUrl = 'https://fntx.modone.me/';
const orgId = 'https://fntx.modone.me/#organization';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    '@id': `${url}#webpage`,
    url,
    name: t.seo.about.title,
    description: t.seo.about.description,
    inLanguage: 'en',
    mainEntity: { '@id': orgId },
    isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://fntx.modone.me/#website' },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    '@id': `${url}#breadcrumb`,
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: homeUrl },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  currentPath="about"
  title={t.seo.about.title}
  description={t.seo.about.description}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 px-4 py-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 sm:px-6 dark:text-slate-400">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: t.breadcrumb.home, href: homeUrl }, { label: t.footer.links.about }]} />

    <header class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
        About Fntx Web
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Last updated: November 26, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Font files are often far larger than a website needs, and the formats are confusing. Most
        online tools solve this by asking you to upload the file to a server. For a paid or
        custom-made font, that is a hard thing to agree to.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fntx Web takes the other path: everything runs inside your browser. You can shrink, convert
        and merge fonts without handing them to anyone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What you can do here</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Inspect a font: name, format, character coverage, size.</li>
        <li>Shrink a font to only the characters your page uses.</li>
        <li>Convert between TTF, WOFF2, WOFF, OTF, EOT and SVG.</li>
        <li>Split a font collection (TTC) into single fonts, or pack fonts into one.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Why everything stays local</h2>
      <p>
        Your font is loaded into the browser’s memory and processed there. Nothing is uploaded, and
        generated files are created on your device. This is a design choice, not a setting: there is
        no upload endpoint to disable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How it works</h2>
      <p>
        The processing engine is written in Rust, compiled to WebAssembly, and runs in a background
        Web Worker so large fonts do not freeze the page. The site itself is a static build, which
        keeps hosting simple and fast.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Honest limits</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Very large CJK fonts can use a lot of memory. On phones, close other tabs first.</li>
        <li>Conversion changes the container, not the design. It cannot add glyphs a font never had.</li>
        <li>Results depend on the source font. Keeping a backup of the original is always wise.</li>
        <li>Font licenses still apply. Check that shrinking, converting or republishing is allowed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Open source and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Fntx Web is an independent open-source project. The code, issue tracker and release history
        live on GitHub, which is also the best place to report a bug or suggest a feature.
      </p>
      <p>
        {githubUrl ? (
          <a
            href={githubUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-slate-100"
          >
            Visit the project on GitHub
          </a>
        ) : (
          <span>Contact details will be published here when available.</span>
        )}
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>